/// Consent copy for the PESO JobKonek prototype.
/// This version is intentionally labelled as a prototype until the responsible
/// LGU confirms its data-controller identity, DPO contact and retention schedule.
const pesoPrivacyNoticeVersion = 'prototype-2026-10-23';

const pesoTermsAndConditionsText =
    '''PESO JOBKONEK — TERMS AND CONDITIONS (PROTOTYPE)

1. Accurate information. Provide truthful, current information and submit only documents and personal information that belong to you or that you are authorized to provide.

2. Account security. Keep your password and sign-in methods private. Tell the responsible office if you suspect unauthorized account access. Do not impersonate another applicant or attempt to access another person's profile, resume, NSRP form or application.

3. Employment-service purpose. JobKonek displays saved job notices, helps organize resume/NSRP information, and provides job-compatibility guidance. You must independently confirm a vacancy's availability, location, schedule, requirements and application instructions with PESO or the employer.

4. No hiring guarantee. Compatibility scores, extraction results, recommendations and generated explanations are advisory only. They are not proof of eligibility and do not guarantee an interview, referral, employment or hiring. Official residency verification, referral and hiring decisions remain with authorized PESO staff and employers.

5. Acceptable use. Do not upload unlawful, misleading, malicious, unrelated or third-party documents without authority. Do not interfere with the service, attempt to bypass access controls, or use another person's information to obtain an employment-service benefit.

6. Prototype status. This notice and the application are not a substitute for the Municipality's approved policies. Do not submit real applicant data until the responsible office has approved the official privacy notice, legal bases, data-protection contact and records-retention schedule.

7. Updates. The responsible operator may update these terms and must notify users of material changes before relying on a new version.''';

const pesoPrivacyNoticeText = '''PESO JOBKONEK — PRIVACY NOTICE (PROTOTYPE)
Version: prototype-2026-10-23

IMPORTANT: This is a prototype notice awaiting formal approval by the responsible local government unit. Do not enter real applicant information until the Municipality has confirmed the official data controller, designated Data Protection Officer (DPO), legal bases and records-retention schedule.

1. WHO IS RESPONSIBLE?
Intended public-service office: Municipality of Rodriguez (Montalban), Rizal — Public Employment Service Office (PESO), subject to formal confirmation by the Municipality. A published general municipal contact is municipalityofmontalban@gmail.com, Municipal Hall, Barangay Balite, Rodriguez (Montalban), Rizal. This is a general municipal contact, not a verified DPO-specific address. The Municipality must publish the designated DPO's name and contact details before production use.

2. WHAT INFORMATION MAY BE PROCESSED?
Depending on what you provide and which features you use, the system may process your name, email, phone number, account identifier, barangay and residential address, residency-review evidence and status, date of birth and derived age, sex, religion, education, work history, occupation preferences, skills, certificates, resume, NSRP Form 1, signature, profile photo, screening answers, application history, language/settings preferences, submitted feedback, security events and service diagnostics. Date of birth, age, religion, education and some other fields may be sensitive personal information under the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (RA 10173).

3. WHY IS IT USED?
The intended purposes are to create and secure your account; store the resume and NSRP information you choose to submit; show saved job opportunities; review Montalban residency eligibility; receive and manage applications; support PESO referrals and authorized employer review; provide user-requested resume extraction, translation and job-compatibility guidance; maintain service security; and produce authorized operational reports. Information should be limited to what is necessary for each purpose. The Municipality must approve the applicable lawful basis for each processing activity; this prototype notice does not assert that consent alone is the legal basis for every government service.

4. AI, MATCHING AND HUMAN REVIEW
If you request AI extraction or translation, relevant resume/profile text or job-description content may be processed by Google Gemini. The Go Mini-AI compares work-related information such as skills, education, experience and occupation categories with saved job criteria. Results may be incomplete or incorrect and are advisory only. They must not be treated as an official eligibility or hiring decision. Authorized people at PESO and employers remain responsible for official residency, referral and hiring decisions; no hiring decision is intended to be made solely by the AI score.

5. WHO MAY RECEIVE THE INFORMATION?
Access is intended for the applicant who owns the account and authorized PESO administrators who need information for account support, residency review, document review, reporting or application processing. Relevant information may be shared with an employer for an application or referral you initiate. Service providers may process data to operate authentication, hosting, database storage and AI features, including Firebase/Google services, the configured MongoDB hosting provider, Vercel hosting and Google Gemini when its features are used. Information may also be disclosed where required by law or valid legal process. The responsible operator must confirm appropriate contracts, access controls, transfer safeguards and the final list of processors before production.

6. WHERE IS IT STORED AND HOW LONG?
The application is designed to use Firebase Authentication, a MongoDB-backed API, private document storage, hosting services and encrypted local drafts where supported. Production storage locations and transfer arrangements must be confirmed by the responsible operator. Records must be kept only for the period necessary for the stated purpose, applicable law and the Municipality's approved records-retention and disposal schedule. No approved, published retention schedule for this prototype has been verified; the Municipality must set and disclose concrete retention periods and disposal procedures before production. Data must not be kept indefinitely merely because future use is possible.

7. SECURITY
The application uses authenticated accounts, server-side ownership and role checks, and private document access controls. Encrypted local draft storage is used where supported. Production deployment must use secure transport and appropriate organizational, physical and technical safeguards. No online service can promise absolute security; suspected unauthorized access should be reported promptly to the responsible office.

8. YOUR RIGHTS
Subject to applicable law and any lawful exceptions, you may ask to be informed about processing; request access to your personal information and relevant processing details; dispute and correct inaccurate information; object to processing or withdraw consent where consent is the applicable basis; request erasure or blocking and data portability where available; and seek damages or lodge a complaint with the National Privacy Commission. Some records may need to be retained or processed where another lawful basis or government-records obligation applies. The responsible office should explain how to make and appeal a request.

9. HOW TO MAKE A PRIVACY REQUEST OR COMPLAINT
For this prototype, contact the Municipality through municipalityofmontalban@gmail.com or the Municipal Hall, Barangay Balite, Rodriguez (Montalban), Rizal, and ask to be directed to the designated Data Protection Officer. This is not a substitute for publishing the DPO's direct contact details. You may also consult the National Privacy Commission's official resources at https://privacy.gov.ph/data-subject-rights/ and https://privacy.gov.ph/the-right-to-be-informed/.

10. CHANGES AND APPROVAL
Material changes to purposes, recipients, AI processing or retention must be communicated before the revised processing is relied on. Before real applicants use this service, the Municipality must formally approve this notice; confirm the controller and DPO; define legal bases for each purpose; set retention and deletion schedules; verify provider agreements and transfers; and provide an official request/complaint process.''';
